---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">UN SDG 7 · Affordable and Clean Energy</span>
      <h1>Georgia Tech runs on power.<br />Help decide where it comes from.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        For Georgia Tech undergraduates in any major who want real experience on a problem that affects every
        building you walk into. Campus energy is one of the biggest challenges Tech has committed to solve, and students
        are part of the solution.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved">Find your way in</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-it-matters">Why it matters</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Campus energy, by the numbers</h2>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>$34.9M</strong>
          <p>Georgia Tech's energy bill in FY2025, up 15% from the year before.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>&lt;1%</strong>
          <p>Share of campus energy produced by on-site solar.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-tile">
          <strong>50%</strong>
          <p>Cut in emissions Georgia Tech has committed to by 2030, on the way to net-zero by 2050.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        Sources:
        <a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/files/2026/02/Georgia-Tech-2025-Annual-Utility-Report-Final-1.pdf">GT FY2025 Annual Utility Report</a>;
        <a href="https://sustain.gatech.edu/2024/04/05/climate-action-plan-provides-road-map-to-net-zero-emissions/">GT Climate Action Plan</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Why you should care</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">1</div>
          <h3>It's your campus</h3>
          <p>
            Electricity is Georgia Tech's single largest source of emissions. The choices made about labs, dorms, and
            classrooms over the next few years decide whether Tech meets its 2030 goal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">2</div>
          <h3>It's your career</h3>
          <p>
            Energy touches every field: engineering, computing, business, policy, and design. Campus projects build the
            skills employers in this growing field are hiring for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="num">3</div>
          <h3>It's already happening</h3>
          <p>
            Students have audited campus buildings, raced solar cars, and pitched carbon cuts to employers. Their work
            is shaping real upgrades. You don't need to be an expert to start.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">See it on campus</span>
        <h2>A building that makes more energy than it uses</h2>
        <p>
          The Kendeda Building for Innovative Sustainable Design, next to the EcoCommons, produced <strong>194%</strong>
          of its own electricity in FY2025 from its rooftop solar canopy. It shows what campus energy could look like,
          and anyone can tour it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Watch how the solar canopy closed the gap to net-positive energy, then see the
          <a href="/get-involved">ways you can help bring that thinking to the rest of campus</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="video">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/W134QA1mFpY"
          title="Solar: The Last Step For Net-Positive Energy at The Kendeda Building"
          loading="lazy"
          allow="accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          allowfullscreen></iframe>
        <p class="cite">Video: The Kendeda Building (YouTube).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start with one step this week.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Take the two-question quiz on our Get Involved page to match with a club, team, job, or one-hour event that fits
        your schedule and interests.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved#quiz">Take the quiz</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/resources">Browse resources</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero,
  .cta {
    background:
      radial-gradient(900px 400px at 85% -10%, rgba(179, 163, 105, 0.35), transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(160deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--navy-deep) 100%);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 12vw, 8rem) 0;
  }
  .hero h1,
  .cta h2 {
    color: #fff;
  }
  .hero .eyebrow {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .hero .lead,
  .cta .lead {
    color: #cfdbe7;
  }
</style>
